    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58157" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνῆσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνάω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>scratching</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῖψις καὶ κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phlb.</u>
					46d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. κροτάφων καὶ ὤτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>CA</u>
					1.1
				</span></i>
			: pl., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				51d
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>tickling</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕνεκα . . κνήσεως ὤτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.167b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (from 
				Pass.
			) <i>itching, irritation</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. περὶ τὰ οὖλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					251c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				10.437
			</span></i>.</div>
